      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Problems of Indian Agriculture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s5ddw1b",
      "content": "• Small land holdings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d4e34ak",
      "content": "• Dependence on monsoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z9k117s",
      "content": "• Low productivity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gt75ljy",
      "content": "• Lack of modern technology."
    },
    {
      "id": "mhuhe28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Government Initiatives"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinction between Kharif crops (sown June-July, e.g., Rice, Cotton) and Rabi crops (sown Oct-Dec, e.g., Wheat, Mustard) is a high-frequency exam topic.",
        "Dr. M.S. Swaminathan is recognized as the Father of the Green Revolution in India, while Norman Borlaug is recognized globally.",
        "Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) focuses on the motto 'Har Khet Ko Pani' and 'More Crop Per Drop'."
      ],
      "id": "u0o7wwz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xsjbv5p",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana – crop insurance scheme."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "apwtxcg",
      "content": "• Soil Health Card Scheme – improves soil fertility."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a3ji723",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana – irrigation development."
    },
    {
      "id": "xtd3ngv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tjbykyr",
      "content": "• Kharif crops are sown with the onset of monsoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2tcedp8",
      "content": "• Punjab and Haryana benefited most from Green Revolution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gk4l47e",
      "content": "• Rice is the staple food crop of India."
    }
